# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/octo-3 window (octo-T8 and its three levers on the fused stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/octo-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq arm needs its binary; every other arm runs that
# binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C1 (TIMED, the CONTROL of the first ABAB pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all, the fused stack as it runs today (two M3 blocks, W2, engine reuse,
# every fusion lever), eight live (concurrent8_steady), eight at 32k and 120k with 800-token answers (concurrent8_code_32k / _128k) and eight at depth for the whole
# all-live window (concurrent8_code_32k_long, concurrent8_code_128k_long). Every boot a fresh reset. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt,
# ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. The two _long tests are this window's DEEP tests: eight real-code prompts of about 32k / 120k tokens with budgets
# (3,000 / 4,000, ignore_eos) that outlast the prefill queue, so that the last user arrives while the first is still decoding and eight seats decode together at depth; the
# 800-token concurrent8_code_32k / _128k (run beside them for continuity) never have six seats live at once, so no octo round runs in them and they read NO LOSS below six
# live seats. The octo-2 card runs' "bundle 4% slower at 32k" was exactly that: no octo round in the test at all, and a thread race that put the last arrival's decode alone
# at 51 or 31 tok/s. READ: c2_smoke_check clean, no stall; this log is the reference of L1 (octo_compare.py --control <this smoke log> --octo <L1 smoke log>: every answer
# equal, user by user) and of the floor (C1 against C2). TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a
# second through the smoke step; read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A gain that comes
# with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 65 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo3-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k,concurrent8_code_32k_long,concurrent8_code_128k_long
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=100
